 Russian history following the dissolution of the Soviet Union. Drafted by Sergey Shakhray, it established the framework for the Russian Federation's governmental structure, enshrining principles of democracy and the rule of law. This constitution is not only significant for its legal content but also for the symbolic break it represented from decades of communist rule, marking a shift toward more Western-oriented governance in Eastern Europe.

